  "result": "Perfect! All 49 tests pass (34 existing + 15 new). Here's what I added:\n\n**`addLine(invoice, { sku, qty })`** \u2014 modifies a draft invoice\n- Adds a new line at the end, or increments qty if the SKU already exists\n- Enriches new lines with product data (name, unitPrice, vatRate)\n- Validates qty is a positive integer (returns `QTY_INVALID`)\n- Validates SKU exists in catalogue (returns `UNKNOWN_SKU`)\n- Rejects non-draft invoices (returns `NOT_DRAFT`)\n- Never mutates the input\n\n**`removeLine(invoice, sku)`** \u2014 modifies a draft invoice\n- Removes the line with that SKU\n- Returns `LINE_NOT_FOUND` if SKU not on invoice\n- Returns `NO_LINES` if it would remove the last line (invoices must have \u22651 line)\n- Rejects non-draft invoices (returns `NOT_DRAFT`)\n- Never mutates the input\n\n**New error codes** added to `src/errors.js`:\n- `NOT_DRAFT`: \"This invoice is no longer in draft status.\"\n- `LINE_NOT_FOUND`: \"No line with that SKU on this invoice.\"\n\n**Tests** (15 new ones) cover:\n- Adding new lines and incrementing existing ones\n- Data enrichment for new lines\n- Validation of input (qty, SKU, status)\n- Edge cases (removing last line, missing SKU)\n- Non-mutation guarantees\n- Integration between both functions",
